<title>GERMANY: Deutsche says plans no capital raise.</title>
<headline>Deutsche says plans no capital raise.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG said on Wednesday that while it intended to make changes to its equity structure, it did not plan an increase in its capital.</p>
<p>Finance chief Juergen Krumnow also told the interim results news conference that the bank planned to have its accounts according to the IAS international accounting standard approved by the New York stock exchange by the year 2000.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
